  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="11">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Northu">Northu</ref> 11</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="11" corresp="#wit-d">Gif pr<hi rend="italic">eost</hi> folce miswissige æt freolse oððe fæstene, bete wið God ⁊ gilde XII ór.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-d">Gif preost folce miswissige æt freolse oððe fæstene, bete wið God and gilde XII or.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock" corresp="#wit-d">If a priest misdirect the people regarding a festival or a fast, he is to make amends to God and pay 12 ores.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-d">If a priest misleads the people concerning a holy day or a fast, he is to do penance before God and pay twelve oras.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Wenn ein Pfarrer die Gemeinde missleitet betreffend Feiertag oder Fasten, büsse er geistlich und zahle 12 Ör.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If a priest misleads the people about a feast-day or fast, let him atone with God and pay 12 ores.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="381"><ref target="clause:EGu_3-1">EGu 3.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. E Gu. 3, 1</note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares EGu 3.1.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
